A||N||16||Monkeyman||MR2 seats in a Fiero?||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||10-28-2001||06:31 AM||||Just noticed an interior shot of a 1<sup>st</sup> generation MR2 in the Fiero Performance Portfolio.  The MR2 seats look to be leather with tons of adjustments (manual, but that saves space).  Anyone know if those would fit in a Fiero?  Or are they too wide?  (The Fiero is wider than the MR2 but with a wider console.)  I don't have any access to the seats, but I think I could buy some if they'd work well.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||10-28-2001||07:09 AM||||I sat in an MR2 at a car lot once and found the seats nice.  I was looking for something different.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Could never find a set that wasn't trashed. I wanted to reduce that headrest that blocks the rear window.  I ended up with a pair of 91 Prelude buckets.  They are pretty comfy, but just a tiny bit of a squeeze with the console.  Makes the interior look a lot different.<BR>Gary||||reg||6
Z||000002||Monkeyman||10-28-2001||07:12 AM||||Got any pics of your new seats?  I can't afford to get any seats wider than the stock seats as my custom center console is just a touch wider than stock.  I'm rubbing slightly the way it is.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||10-28-2001||09:42 AM||||This is a test fit in my SE.  I'll try to post them in the black GT.  I'm building a slightly narrower console.<P>They will rub on a stock ECM cover.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seats.jpg"> <BR>Gary||||reg||6
Z||000004||Uaana||10-28-2001||11:18 AM||||I was looking at doing the same thing once. <BR>Found that the biggest hurdle for me would be the mounting rails. The Fiero rails are 13 1/2 in apart and the ones on the MR2 seats are like 17 1/4. The seats work fit wise as long as youre not too tall.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||10-28-2001||01:08 PM||||What makes the MR2 seats too tall.  The runners or the seat itself?  If it's just the runners, that can be worked out.  There's gotta be a way to adapt the stock Fiero runners to the MR2 seats (or any other seats for that matter).  All it takes is some imagination.<P>FieroBUZZ--If they rub on the stock ECM cover, then there's no way they'd work in my car.  I'd still like to see some better shots of them.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jaei Sun||10-28-2001||04:08 PM||||MR2=BAD THERE RICE CRAP DONT RIUN A GOOD FEIRO WITH JAPCRAP!!11!!  <P>j/k<P>Seriously I would like to see 2nd gen MR2 seats in a fiero.. they're really comfortable plenty of lumbar support.||||reg||1
Z||000007||AusFiero||10-28-2001||04:33 PM||||I just measured my 2 gen MR2 seats MM and they are 49cm or 19.6" wide at their widest point on the base and on the backrest. Hope that helps you out. If you can find some second generation MR2 ones they are really comfortable.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
