Z||000014||286SE'S||10-30-2001||03:31 PM||||I bought a pair of 1st generation MR2 seats from the junkyard. The rails are bizarre to say the least. There is an X shaped support beam in the car and they bolt to the sides of the beams at odd angles. I never considered them for my Fiero because they were blue, just for resale (they were in excellent condition) They have a knob only on the drivers side that adjusts the lumbar (lower back) support and there is a lever that moves the side supports in or out for a cozy fit. If you could solve the rail problems (they are integrated in to the design) they would be comfortable seat. ||||reg||7
